 "path_rule": "corrected rule (sponsor, 2026-11-25 10:04 EST): flow = presynaptic activation times weight over the fixed 200-problem validation set; a weight synapse passes iff its flow std is at least half the largest flow std among the weight synapses feeding the same node; the main path is the passing synapses on a connected entry-to-exit route (routes may step through the residual and attention/logit conduits, which are structural connectors, not competitors). The generalised machinery was validated against stitch #2: run on species 8 and 9 it reproduces the recorded path sets exactly (13 and 26 synapses).",
 "attn_scale": {
  "value": 0.7071067811865475,
  "why": "the engine's initial-arch scale at d=2 (arch.attn_scale of be.initial_arch(cfg, 2)). Species 10's native arch is d=2, and the Frankenstein 4 champion's evolution forward pass used this same value for every block's attention and for the decoder logits; the squared network keeps it so every copied weight retains the scale it was built/evolved under. It is used for all three blocks' attention and the decoder logits, as in every earlier build."
 },
 "joining_ffn_width_reading": "the joining block's FFN width = the sum of the two sides' FFN path widths, each side's width counted in the block that feeds the joining block on that side (side A: its block 2, 4 units; side B: its block 1, 1 units) = 5, which equals the squared block-2 FFN width \u2014 the same relation as stitches #2/#4, where the joining FFN width equalled the preceding block's FFN width.",
